#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
swarm-review — fan out a review to frontier models in parallel.

Default backend: auto — cursor-agent first (free Cursor credits), with a
fast PIVOT to the direct APIs (xAI, Google, OpenRouter) the moment cursor is
blocked: the ~/.cursor/cli-config.json write-race under heavy parallelism,
or quota exhaustion. The API path has no shared filesystem state, so it is
the parallel-safe escape. Force a single backend with --backend cursor|api.

Reviewer roster is chosen by --preset (NOT auto-detected — explicit over
implicit). Two presets, each a fixed all-free-cursor lineup:
  code  — Codex-5.3-High, Grok-4.5, Gemini-3.1-Pro, Sonnet-4.6
  prose — GPT-5.5, Sonnet-4.6, Gemini-3.1-Pro, Kimi-K3
The split is surfaced to operators as two skills (/swarm-review-code,
/swarm-review-prose) that each pin a preset; this engine is shared.

Usage:
  swarm-review --preset code file.py [file2.go ...]   review files (code roster)
  swarm-review --preset prose plan.md                 review files (prose roster)
  swarm-review --preset code --git-diff               review git diff vs HEAD
  swarm-review --preset code --git-diff --staged      review staged changes only
  cat draft.md | swarm-review --preset prose --stdin  review piped content
  swarm-review --preset code --backend api file.go    force direct APIs
  swarm-review --preset code --backend auto file.go   cursor → API fallback
  swarm-review --preset code --no-sonnet --focus "security" auth.go

Generate mode (offensive — fan a brief out for original analysis, not review):
  swarm-review --mode generate -q "Make the case for X"     fan a brief to the prose roster
  swarm-review --mode generate -q "..." background.md ref.md attach reference context
  echo "the brief" | swarm-review --mode generate --stdin   pipe the brief
  swarm-review --mode generate --preset code -q "..."       use the coding roster instead
"""

